From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:36:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] logging_chrome: register no ETW provider for log messages

On Windows, InitChromeLogging registered Chromium's ETW log provider
({7FE69228-633E-4f06-80C1-527FEA23E3A7}). Any trace session that enables
it receives every log message of every browser process, and lowers the
processes' minimum log level to its own. Windows telemetry's DiagTrack
sessions (WPR_initiated_DiagTrackMiniLogger_OneTrace_*) enable it at the
verbose level, and many log messages carry URLs and host names; on the
reference machine it made every process log at VERBOSE1, which also pushed
browser tests over the test launcher's output limit. Shade registers none;
--enable-logging still writes a log file.

Why: no switch or pref controls the registration; it happens in InitChromeLogging for every process.
Upstream: not upstreamable: Chrome's developers rely on ETW tracing
Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/chrome/common/logging_chrome.cc b/chrome/common/logging_chrome.cc
index b6d6fc87bdf137a35207acb750a03d18ffaaaff7..73108a0e9f74376aa10fb3a6e2f810ee90af24a1 100644
--- a/chrome/common/logging_chrome.cc
+++ b/chrome/common/logging_chrome.cc
@@ -81,15 +81,6 @@ bool chrome_logging_redirected_ = false;
 constexpr char kChronosHomeDir[] = "/home/chronos/user/";
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
-// {7FE69228-633E-4f06-80C1-527FEA23E3A7}
-const GUID kChromeTraceProviderName = {
-    0x7fe69228,
-    0x633e,
-    0x4f06,
-    {0x80, 0xc1, 0x52, 0x7f, 0xea, 0x23, 0xe3, 0xa7}};
-#endif
-
 // Assertion handler for logging errors that occur when dialogs are
 // silenced.  To record a new error, pass the log string associated
 // with that error in the str parameter.
@@ -514,8 +505,10 @@ void InitChromeLogging(const base::CommandLine& command_line,
   }
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
-  // Enable trace control and transport through event tracing for Windows.
-  LogEventProvider::Initialize(kChromeTraceProviderName);
+  // Shade registers no ETW provider for its log messages: a trace session
+  // that enables one receives every message and lowers the minimum log
+  // level to its own, and Windows telemetry's DiagTrack sessions enable
+  // Chromium's at the verbose level. --enable-logging still writes a file.
 
   // Enable logging to the Windows Event Log.
   SetEventSource(base::WideToASCII(
